+++ b/README.md
@@ -36,3 +36,19 @@ move into the value's own child, or a `test` that does not match (deep equality,
 A failing patch has no partial effect. Removing the whole document (`remove` with path `""`) is rejected,
 as no JSON value would remain. Unrecognized members of an operation are ignored. Paths follow the same
 pointer rules as `resolvePointer`, so `__proto__` is an ordinary member and prototypes are never reached.
+
+## JSON Merge Patch (RFC 7386)
+
+`applyMergePatch(target, patch)`, exported from `src/index.ts`, applies a merge patch to a target document
+and returns the merged document as a new value.
+
+```ts
+applyMergePatch({ a: "b", c: { d: "e" } }, { a: "z", c: { d: null } }); // { a: "z", c: {} }
+```
+
+An object patch is merged member by member: `null` removes the member, an object merges recursively and
+any other value (arrays included) replaces it. A patch that is not an object replaces the whole target,
+and a non-object target is treated as `{}` when an object patch is applied. As the format dictates, a
+merge patch cannot set a member to `null`. It never throws. Neither argument is mutated, and the result
+shares no structure with them. Only own members are read and `__proto__` is an ordinary member, so
+prototypes are never reached.
